  "title": "Spread of Islam across Africa and Asia",
  "summary": "After Arab Muslims conquered North Africa in the 7th century, Islam spread through West Africa largely peacefully, via merchants, traders, scholars and missionaries, reaching the Mali and Songhai empires. Arab traders carried it to East Africa and the Swahili Coast. In Southeast Asia, Islamic port city-states ruled by sultans appear by the 13th century, among them Pasai in Sumatra.",
